## Frequently asked questions

### Does Google treat healthcare websites differently?

Yes. YMYL pages need demonstrable expertise, clear author credentials and accurate content that qualified practitioners have authored or reviewed.

### Who writes the medical content?

Your clinicians author or review the medical content. I provide the search structure, briefs, schema and technical work. The provider keeps responsibility for clinical accuracy and approval.

### How do you measure healthcare SEO?

I measure healthcare SEO through enquiries, calls, bookings and visibility for service and location terms. I never use clinical outcomes as an SEO performance measure.

### What is GEO for private clinics?

GEO means making a clinic easier for AI assistants to find, check and cite when patients ask for recommendations. For clinics it rests on named clinical reviewers, accurate registration details, consistent facts across the web and careful treatment claims.

### Can you guarantee my clinic appears in ChatGPT answers?

No. AI answers vary by assistant, prompt and user. I measure your visibility with a fixed prompt panel. I work on the evidence assistants rely on and never promise a mention.

